{"id":"7d4b6268983ed1698445792738ae442b921c54b4","axis":"silent","repo":"pnpm/pnpm","sha":"7d4b6268983ed1698445792738ae442b921c54b4","parsed":{"files":[{"path":".changeset/pnpr-web-login.md","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,5 @@","+---","+\"@pnpm/pnpr\": patch","+---","+","+Added the login web flow (`/-/v1/login`) so `npm login` and `pnpm login` authenticate via browser SSO when an OIDC login provider is configured."],"additions":5,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"pnpm/crates/cli/tests/suite/python/indexes.rs","lines":["@@ -82,6 +82,7 @@ async fn selected_registry_errors_do_not_fall_back_to_another_index() {","     let denied = extra","         .mock(\"GET\", \"/simple/alpha/\")","         .with_status(403)","+        .expect_at_least(1)","         .create_async()","         .await;","     project(root.path(), &primary.url(), &[\"alpha\"]);"],"additions":1,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"pnpm/crates/network/src/certificates.rs","lines":["@@ -28,7 +28,8 @@ pub(super) enum TrustRoots {"," /// [`Certificate`] form. Parsed once — `for_installs` builds one"," /// client per per-registry override, and the fallback path is taken"," /// by every one of them on a system without a trust store.","-pub(super) fn bundled_root_certs() -> &'static [Certificate] {","+#[must_use]","+pub fn bundled_root_certs() -> &'static [Certificate] {","     static CERTS: LazyLock<Vec<Certificate>> = LazyLock::new(|| {","         webpki_root_certs::TLS_SERVER_ROOT_CERTS","             .iter()"],"additions":2,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"pnpm/crates/network/src/lib.rs","lines":["@@ -13,6 +13,7 @@ pub use auth::{","     nerf_dart, normalize_auth_key, redact_and_sanitize, redact_and_sanitize_multiline,","     redact_npm_auth_key, redact_url_credentials, redact_url_for_display,"," };","+pub use certificates::bundled_root_certs;"," pub use client_builder::{default_network_concurrency, native_dns_resolver};"," pub use error_chain::{is_permanent_error, walk_reqwest_chain};"," pub use